			<div class="content" id="post-content-4811513">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Love, Drama/Emotional, Action, Mystery (Mild)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>This is a longer article.</strong></li>
<li>Short containment procedure and description, as the anomalies are neutralized.</li>
<li><strong>The idea of the story is that the addendums tell the story.</strong> <em>Kind of like SCP-1730.</em></li>
<li>Serpent’s Hand = SH | The Gate Guardian = GG</li>
<li><strong>I will definitely be missing certain aspects of the story, based on the 400 word limit.</strong></li>
<li>If you wish to understand some aspects of this thread, <strong>please look through the post below titled “Explaining My Plot Holes”</strong> to understand the tone of my concept.</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Tab&nbsp;For&nbsp;Space</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">My&nbsp;Concept/Idea</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br /></p>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p><strong>How far will someone go for love?</strong><br />
<em>Because Orpheus was the only one willing <span style="text-decoration: underline;">To Go Hell And Back</span> for his beloved&#8230;</em></p>
</div>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The anomaly is a deceased female that is being preserved using advanced cryogenics. She is anomalously beautiful, with every man viewing her differently but all agreeing that she is extremely beautiful. She also had the ability to change the state of matter around her hands, wearing black gloves to control her ability. She is O5-2, who was killed by the SH while secretly getting married with her husband.</p>
<p>The Foundation investigates her death and after the events described below, an event log was created.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
Essentially O5-2, Eurydice, secretly dated an anomalous musician named Orpheus, a former member of the SH. To prevent the Council from knowing of her affair, Eurydice barely uses Foundation resources to prevent suspicions. Not to mention, Eurydice hides her troops to keep a shellshocked Orpheus as comfortable as possible. The SH, wanting to tie up loose ends, planned to kill Orpheus and use Eurydice as a bargaining chip to get certain anomalies from the Foundation. They launch a multi-pronged assault, with Eurydice sacrificing herself to save Orpheus and allowing him to escape.</p>
<p>Rather than fighting the SH, <em>he plans on resurrecting Eurydice</em>. He uses his harp to disguise himself and enter Site-19 to ask SCP-343 “how to resurrect Eurydice.” SCP-343 tells him that “it requires the convincing of the Arch-Drudgeon,” something SCP-343 doesn’t want to get involved with. After this discussion, the Foundation are able to follow Orpheus. He establishes a plan to convince JALAKARA in resurrecting Eurydice, entering The Wanderer’s Library to find “The Song of Minor.” He encounters the SH and subdues Cerberus to obtain the song. Orpheus begins traveling to Site 0.</p>
<p>He arrives to Site 0 and uses a verse to please the GG, with the GG leading Orpheus through the gate and directly to JALAKARA’s doorstep. JALAKARA is obviously pissed, but Orpheus sings the song and is given a chance to resurrect Eurydice. He does his famous trial and fails, dragging Eurydice’s dead body out of the gate. He is attacked by the SH, in which he allows himself to be ripped apart by the group and dies to the wounds.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
The Foundation obtains the body dragged out by Orpheus, trying everything to resurrect the O5-2.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

