			<div class="content" id="post-content-4811970">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Only&nbsp;look&nbsp;if&nbsp;you’re&nbsp;-ebonbonb-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;List&nbsp;of&nbsp;Things&nbsp;for&nbsp;Editing&nbsp;the&nbsp;Thread</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Yes you are right with the cohesiveness and the several plot holes on my article. A few things I need to point out.</p>
<p>I should have listed this above in that a majority of the addendums are retrieved files, emails, or audio logs from personnel of the GoIs. It’s kind of like all these events are occurring and happening so fast that the Foundation is essentially playing catch up by surveying the damage.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This article is more of a collection of different files, logs, and emails with the Foundation piecing the whole story. A reference is SCP-5555, where a series of video logs, emails, and notes tell the story.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like the important thing is that this article is the first instance of the SCP Foundation and the major Groups of Interest finally giving basic civil rights to reality benders, treating them as people rather than as an anomalous item.<br />
Now that I got that out of the way, I feel like I can respond to the discrepancies that you gave<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-635444-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-635444-1')">1</a></sup>.</p>
<hr />
<ol>
<li>Yes, the anomalous event does involve the harp. It’s a fight between the bad GoIs and Orpheus.</li>
<li>Again, I should have broken this down more effectively. When I mean by civilian casualties, the civilians are of Three Portlands. The anomalous event explained on #1 is the first event that occurs outside of Three Portlands, while all the death is occurring in Three Portlands. This is kind of why the Foundation, TMI, and the UIU are barely finding out. <em>This war is involving the battle for civil rights that I later described. The narrative is that Orpheus was once a part of the civil rights movement, but gave it up for Eurydice. It’s kind of like his past life is coming back to haunt him.</em></li>
<li>In turn, I felt like the GOC is used incorrectly in the first version. I feel like D.C al Fine is not directly involved, but more like the Serpent’s Hand is influencing her (like with mind control of sorts). She is allowing the GOC to help the Serpent’s Hand and Chaos Insurgency but I do plan on Orpheus killing or subduing her as a reference to the actual myth. I feel like I can change this to make the Serpent’s Hand member the one who loved Orpheus but D.C al Fine is controlled by that girl.</li>
<li>Admittedly the UIU is a side character, kind of referencing the fact that the UIU is infamously lacking in resources to get involved. They are the first to investigate and the UIU are involved with Three Portlands, which is why I felt the need to include them in a way. Besides that they are kind of pushed to the side after Orpheus begins trying to resurrect Eurydice.</li>
<li>The GOC, Serpent’s Hand, and Chaos Insurgency fully agree on giving reality benders civil rights, that is the common goal with the three groups. But how this goal is effective with each group is what makes this a shaky alliance. The Serpent’s Hand is the only group that is committed to this cause, so they are the puppet masters of sorts. The Chao’s Insurgency are willing to utilize reality benders, so by giving them civil rights they are employees rather than tools. This is why the Serpent’s Hand is allying with the Chaos Insurgency. The GOC is a little out of place, but like explained on #3 the Serpent’s Hand can have mild control over D.C al Fine, making the GOC the military body of the alliance. I also feel like I can expand upon this in that while the GOC’s main goal is the destruction of anomalies, the Secret Council of 108 might be convinced to allow reality benders to be people.</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
