			<div class="content" id="post-content-4817513">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>After finding the body of O5-2 and SH members, they quickly let the Foundation take over.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The identity of the O5 council is kept secret; how do the UIU know it's O5-2?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The UIU’s investigation is the only evidence found until SCP-343’s cell is breached, with cameras showing a “shadow” talking to SCP-343 and discussing “how to resurrect immortals.” The Foundation starts retracing O5-2’s steps to see what led up to her death. Before piecing it together, Site 0 sounds the alarms of a breach and sees SCP-001 taking 3 steps away from the gate. A battle ensues between Orpheus and the SH before the Gate Guardian vaporizes the 1km region.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm going to be extremely honest here: this section is too summarised. I don't know how we get from 'shadow talking to 343' to 'foundation linking this to O5-2's steps' to '001 steps away from the gate' to 'battle ensues' at all.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>While the initial plan of killing her was executed, Orpheus deduced that they were SH members.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Surely this should be 'Orpheus deduce that they tricked him' and like&#8230;how did he figure that out?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-343 tells him that it requires “the convincing of The Guardian and the pleasing of the Spider God.”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why does it need the guardian and jalakara? This feels like it's kinda real convoluted for no real reason other than to involve more groups of interest?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>JALAKARA requests the TMI to allow the souls of both Orpheus and Eurydice to leave Corbenic once a year and explore Earth, with the Foundation agreeing to the terms.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>how does JALAKARA have both the souls? did Orpheus not succeed in reviving Eurydice?</p>
<hr />
<p>I think my central concern with this is that, it feels like this is an incredibly complex story but it also doesn't feel interesting? It still has a tonne of moving parts and stuff; but at the end of the day, it's a very detached-ly told love story and I can't help but feel like this would be a lot better as a tale from Orpheus's perspective still.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

