			<div class="content" id="post-content-4812266">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">This&nbsp;post&nbsp;is&nbsp;for&nbsp;reference&nbsp;of&nbsp;possible&nbsp;changes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">No&nbsp;need&nbsp;to&nbsp;look&nbsp;here</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So I made a bunch of changes that differs from my original concept. Here is a list of the changes I have made.</p>
<ul>
<li>It was noted that the 6 anomalous groups make the story muddy, especially that the main focus is suppose to be Orpheus and Eurydice. So <strong>I decided to divide the whole thing into two different stories.</strong> This is described above in the page layout.</li>
<li>The goals of the Serpent’s Hand, GOC, and the Chaos Insurgency are different but I felt that if <strong>they all agreed on a common consensus they were willing to work with each other.</strong> This is described above.</li>
<li>The story of Orpheus was muddied, but I wanted him to fight the 3 groups with help of the Foundation, so I decided <strong>to reference the original actions of Orpheus from the myth as a way to tie in the idea that the myth occurs.</strong> I explain above the several events that are easily understood.</li>
<li>So I tried to tie in personal motivation to a rights issue, as the group appeared to have used the backdrop of the protest to punctuate the personal gain (that’s even confusing to explain), so <strong>I made it all centered around the protesting of civil rights rather than a duo of personal and social motivation</strong>.</li>
<li>Admittedly, the joint operation get too involved with the actions of Orpheus, kind of influencing him rather than him thinking of how to save Eurydice. I changed this <strong>to make Orpheus use the O5 council to help him. He’s the puppet master of the actions.</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>All in all, I tried to divide the actions of the anomalous groups into one story. The second story is the story of Orpheus, with the anomalous groups as reference.</p>
</div>
